UID:10001068-1792836000-1792843200@bird-in-hand.com
SUMMARY:Make & Take: Glass Christmas Tree
DESCRIPTION:Learn to create a custom piece of seasonal decor \nJust in time for the holidays\, you can learn how to transform ordinary materials into treasured artwork. In this 90-minute workshop\, local artisan Karen Worst will guide you through the process of selecting the glass\, beads and wooden pieces you’ll use to make a still-life picture of a Christmas tree\, putting the pieces together with resin binder and\, finally\, matting and framing your creation to take home. Choose from a variety of colors to match your décor. \nBefore retiring\, Karen Worst worked as a nurse by day and created art in her downtime. Today\, she makes one-of-a-kind\, nature-inspired art with glass\, recycled glass\, resin\, acrylic paint and other simple materials. \nReserve your space today! \n$30 per person includes instruction and all material for framed 6-x-6-inch finished art. \n\nDate: Saturday\, October 24\nTime: 10 a.m.\n\nTo save your space: Limited spots available. Call (717) 344-6875 to reserve your space.
URL:https://bird-in-hand.com/event/make-take-sea-glass-christmas-tree/
LOCATION:Bird-in-Hand Artisan Village\, 2705 Old Philadelphia Pike\, Bird-in-Hand\, PA\, 17505\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bird-in-hand.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ChristmasTreeMT.jpg
END:VEVENT
