UID:10015047-1792845000-1792852200@figlancaster.com
SUMMARY:RegenAll + PCA&D: Exploring Recycled Materials - Landscapes: Grades 1-3
DESCRIPTION:In 2026\, RegenAll’s Youth Climate Art Exhibition will be a pre-event component of RegenAll’s Annual Climate Summit. Students from around the county will have the opportunity to express their vision of a thriving\, resilient\, and sustainable “green future” to promote creative and hopeful thinking for the next generation. We hope that their work will inspire decision-makers\, lawmakers\, and community members to see a better future for our shared environment. The exhibition will be held November 8 – 15 at Pennsylvania College of Art & Design’s Welcome Center (241 N. Prince Street\, Lancaster\, PA ) with an opening reception on Friday\, November 13\, 2026 from 5 – 7:30 pm. \n\n\n\nOne way for young community members to submit work is in one of our free workshops held at PCA&D! Join us! In this workshop\, we will be making a farm or river scene out of recycled materials. The goal for this class is to use our materials to create a fun and cool collage of the scene while we think about ways to continue to recycle and keep our planet healthy. Let’s go experiment with all sorts of random materials we can recycle and reuse to make a really cool landscape!  \n\n\n\nInstructor: Misia Palad Saturday \n\n\n\n\n    Learn More
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/regenall-pcad-exploring-recycled-materials-landscapes-grades-1-3/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/09/41.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Pennsylvania College of Art & Design - Center for Creative Exploration":MAILTO:ce@pcad.edu
END:VEVENT
