SUMMARY:Toddler Pumpkin Guts Sensory Play
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261028T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261028T113000
UID:0c94d8416382f6591d22777f08b48ec3@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Arts & Crafts\, Babies\, Toddlers\n\nGet ready to squish\, sco
 op\, and explore at our Pumpkin Guts Sensory Play event!Designed specifica
 lly for curious toddlers\, this hands-on\, delightfully messy morning invi
 tes little learners to dive headfirst into the textures\, colors\, and sme
 lls of autumn. Instead of just looking at pumpkins\, your child will get t
 o experience them from the inside out! Toddlers can sink their hands into 
 cold\, gooey pumpkin pulp\, and separate the slippery seeds It is the ulti
 mate tactile experience to stimulate brain development\, language skills\,
  and spatial awareness in a supportive\, social environment. Recommended f
 or ages 1-3. Registration is required to make sure every child has a pumpk
 in!What to Wear: Dress for a mess! We highly recommend bringing a change o
 f clothes for your little one\, as pumpkin juice and seeds are bound to en
 d up everywhere.What We Provide: All pumpkins\, kid-friendly scooping tool
 s\, magnifying glasses\, and smocks🌟 What to ExpectHands-on Bins: Table
 s loaded with precut pumpkins for ultimate gooey fun.Fine Motor Tools: Twe
 ezers\, large spoons\, and cups to help toddlers practice grasping and pou
 ring.Mess-Free Options: For little ones who are a bit hesitant about stick
 y textures\, we will also have sealed pumpkin sensory bags so they can squ
 ish and observe without getting their hands dirty.
LOCATION:Eastern Lancaster County\, NHD Activity Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/toddler-pumpkin-guts-sen
 sory-play-204725
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
