BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/century-winnie-pooh-206409"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:A Century of Winnie-the-Pooh
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261207T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261207T190000
UID:773eb913332f0c60ae764841e24b8421@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Presentation\, Everyone\n\nWinnie-the-Pooh is cele
 brating its 100th birthday this year! The stories A.A. Milne created have 
 become classics that are as beloved now as they were when they were first 
 published in October 1926. In celebration of the centennial of Milne’s t
 imeless tales\, join Dr. Sarah Jackson\, Assistant Professor from the Depa
 rtment of Early\, Middle\, and Elementary Education at Millersville Univer
 sity to learn about how these beloved children’s stories have endured as
  they have been translated and adapted countless times since their publica
 tion 100 years ago. Dr. Jackson will focus on the influence of colonialism
  in the stories and consider how the animal characters try on—and resist
 —colonial language. All ages welcome\, but this will be a lecture-style 
 program geared toward the young at heart 😉
LOCATION:Lancaster\, LPL Community Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/century-winnie-pooh-2064
 09
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
