X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Teen Advisory Board
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261214T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261214T190000
UID:fedb376b5a4aef7feb14004f1302c595@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Teens\n\nAre you a teen who loves the library and 
 wants to make a difference? Join our Teen Advisory Board—a new leadershi
 p opportunity for teens to shape library programs\, services\, and spaces!
 As a member\, you’ll:📚 Help plan and promote exciting teen events💡
  Provide input on books\, technology\, and programs you want to see🎤 De
 velop leadership skills and gain volunteer experience🤝 Make friends and
  connect with your communityWe’re looking for passionate\, creative\, an
 d motivated teens (ages 13 - 18) who want to have a voice in making the li
 brary an awesome place for young people.Meetings: Once a month at the libr
 aryPerks: Gain leadership experience\, make an impact\, and if you choose 
 to become a library volunteer\, you can earn volunteer hours!Program Polic
 iesDrop Off Program – This program is intended for children over the age
  of 13 years who can participate independently. Adult(s) must check in wit
 h library staff to provide an emergency contact at their first meeting. Ad
 ults will not be allowed in the event space. Designated Ages – Please ad
 here to the age restrictions designated on your registration. Only childre
 n in that age range will be admitted.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Study Room #119
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-advisory-board-1569
 45
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/hold-adult-services-program-200760"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Coffee & Crossing: Washington's Winter of 1776
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261214T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261214T194500
UID:a2fbea2cd9b3cb07aa1dbe6b0ae172ba@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Presentation\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nGrab a piping-h
 ot mug of authentic colonial coffee and step right into the high-stakes wi
 nter of 1776! Join living historian Samuel Leamer to uncover the bold stra
 tegy\, hidden Lancaster County connections\, and dramatic reality behind W
 ashington’s famous crossing of the Delaware and the epic 1st Battle of T
 renton. Separate fact from fiction\, sip historical brews\, and discover h
 ow coffee and courage helped turn the tide of the Revolutionary War!Regist
 ration is encouraged A Berks County native and Cairn University history gr
 aduate\, Sam Leamer has spent a lifetime bringing the past to life through
  reenactments-- and a decade mastering the art of modern coffee. By blendi
 ng historical scholarship with coffee expertise\, Sam offers a richer\, de
 eper look into Colonial Coffee Culture\, showing how the humble coffee bea
 n helped fuel America’s fight for independence.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center B
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/hold-adult-services-prog
 ram-200760
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
